   "date": "2017-03-21T20:57:27Z",
   "subject": "Centre the Plot Title",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I can use <div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">theme</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">plot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">title </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> element_text</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hjust </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>to centre the plot title, but when I instead try <br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">theme</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">plot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">title </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> element_text</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hjust </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;center&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div></div><div><br></div><div>no title is drawn, and the I get the following warning: </div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Warning</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> messages</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">In</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> unit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;npc&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">NAs</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> introduced </span><span style=\"color:#008\">by</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> coercion <br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">In</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> validDetails</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">text</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">NAs</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> introduced </span><span style=\"color:#008\">by</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> coercion</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>I can use hjust = &#39;center&#39; in other places, like geom_text. </div><div><br></div><div>Is this a bug? </div><br><br><br><br><br><table cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"padding-left:6px;padding-bottom:8px;border-width:initial;border-style:none;outline:none;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);width:1020.5px;font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;!important;font-size:16.4pt!important;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><tbody></tbody></table><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Jws7iqspBQAJ",
   "from": "Olivia",
   "author": "74428f180627b7d7",
   "date": "2017-03-22T19:51:00Z",
   "subject": "Re: Centre the Plot Title",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Running `?element_text()` will pull up the help page for element_text(). You&#39;ll see that it says:<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<br><table cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\">\r\n<p><span>hjust</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\">\r\n<p><span>Horizontal justification (in [0, 1])</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table><div> <br>Suggesting you shouldn&#39;t expect a character string to work for horizontally justifying any element text objects. Other things do use &quot;left&quot; etc etc for justifying, true. Just not this one!</div><div><br></div><div>Kind regards,</div><div><br></div><div>Olivia</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
